BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\) - Incident Response Plan) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 697.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 674.0 Td (This Incident Response Plan \(IRP\) governs how Hewlett Packard Enterprise detects, triages, contains,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660.0 Td (and recovers from cybersecurity incidents across its global infrastructure, cloud platforms, product) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646.0 Td (lines, and corporate networks. It applies to all HPE employees, contractors, and third parties) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632.0 Td (operating within the HPE environment. The plan is owned by the HPE Global Security Operations Center) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (\(SOC\) and is reviewed at least annually or after any material change to the threat landscape.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 592.0 Td (2. Roles and Responsibilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 569.0 Td (HPE operates a follow-the-sun SOC staffed 24x7x365 across three regional hubs, providing continuous) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555.0 Td (monitoring, detection, and first-line triage. The SOC feeds confirmed incidents to the Computer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541.0 Td (Security Incident Response Team \(CSIRT\), HPE's designated incident response team, also referred to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527.0 Td (internally as the Security Incident Response Team \(SIRT\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 507.0 Td (Key roles include:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487.0 Td (- Incident Commander \(IC\) - owns the incident lifecycle end to end, coordinates the response) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 473.0 Td (  team, and authorizes containment actions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459.0 Td (- SOC Analysts \(Tier 1/2/3\) - perform monitoring, alert validation, triage, and escalation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 445.0 Td (- Forensics & Threat Intelligence Lead - directs evidence handling, imaging, and analysis.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 431.0 Td (- Communications & Legal Liaison - manages regulatory notification, customer disclosure, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417.0 Td (  privacy obligations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 403.0 Td (- Executive Sponsor \(CISO delegate\) - engaged for Sev-1 events.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 377.0 Td (3. Incident Classification, Severity, and Priority) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354.0 Td (Every event is assigned a classification and severity/priority rating during triage to drive the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 340.0 Td (appropriate response tempo:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 320.0 Td (| Severity | Description | Example | Target Response |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 307.0 Td (| ---------- | ------------- | --------- | ----------------- |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 294.0 Td (| Sev-1 \(Critical\) | Confirmed breach, active data exfiltration, ransomware, or outage of a customer-facing service | Domain compromise, encryption of production systems | Immediate, IC + executives engaged |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 281.0 Td (| Sev-2 \(High\) | Significant threat with contained blast radius | Targeted phishing with credential theft | < 30 min |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 268.0 Td (| Sev-3 \(Medium\) | Isolated malware or policy violation | Endpoint infection, single-host anomaly | < 4 hours |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 255.0 Td (| Sev-4 \(Low\) | Minor or informational | Reconnaissance, blocked intrusion attempt | < 24 hours |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 236.0 Td (Priority combines severity with business impact and asset criticality. A Sev-1 / critical incident) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222.0 Td (triggers the full call tree and continuous incident bridge until resolution.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 196.0 Td (4. Detection and Triage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 173.0 Td (Detection relies on HPE's SIEM, EDR/XDR telemetry, cloud-native detections, threat intelligence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 159.0 Td (feeds, and user reports to the security mailbox. On alert, the SOC performs initial triage:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 145.0 Td (validating the alert, scoping affected assets, and assigning severity. Confirmed incidents are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131.0 Td (logged in the case management system with a unique incident ID that anchors all subsequent evidence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 117.0 Td (and actions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 91.0 Td (5. Escalation, Notification, and Call Tree) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 68.0 Td (Upon confirmation, the SOC initiates the escalation and notification chain defined in the incident) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
