BT /F2 13 Tf 54 732.0 Td (10. Lessons Learned and Continuous Improvement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 709.0 Td (Within ten business days of resolving a Sev-1 or Sev-2 incident, the CSIRT conducts a post-mortem /) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 695.0 Td (after-action review. This blameless retrospective captures the root cause, timeline, what went well,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681.0 Td (and gaps. Lessons learned are converted into tracked remediation actions, playbook updates, and new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 667.0 Td (detection rules to prevent recurrence.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 641.0 Td (11. Exercises, Drills, and Testing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (The IRP is validated through regular exercises: quarterly tabletop sessions with executives,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 604.0 Td (semi-annual technical drills, and red-team simulations against production-like environments. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590.0 Td (testing confirms the call tree, playbooks, and tooling perform under pressure and that the response) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 576.0 Td (team maintains readiness.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 550.0 Td (12. Plan Maintenance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527.0 Td (This plan is reviewed annually, after major incidents, and following significant exercises. The HPE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513.0 Td (CISO office approves all revisions.) Tj ET
endstream
